-- domain: workouts
-- Coach-facing documentation only — no schema change. Replaces two comments:
--  * protocols: hangboard sessions go in kind='strength' with CARRY/BAR_HOLDS
--    timed holds so the hung load is recorded per set; kind='other' becomes
--    the plain unweighted interval timer.
--  * training_plan: approval is `uv run plan_admin.py approve` (checklist)
--    followed by its publish step; approving alone puts nothing on Garmin.

comment on table training_plan is
'COACH PLANNING TABLE — the coach''s write target. To plan a session, INSERT a row here with run_write_sql: one row = one workout on one date. This is the ONLY way a coach puts a workout on the athlete''s Garmin calendar; never write to workouts or scheduled_workouts. Nothing reaches Garmin until the owner approves AND publishes: after inserting, list the row ids you wrote and tell the athlete to run `uv run plan_admin.py approve` (a checklist: tick rows to approve, optionally rows to cancel, confirm, then answer yes to "Publish approved rows to Garmin now?"), then sync the watch. Approving alone puts nothing on Garmin; rows approved but still status=''planned'' need `uv run plan_admin.py publish`. Two sources: source=''library'' reuses an existing Garmin workout (set exactly one of workout_id — preferred, take it from the workouts table since names repeat — or workout_name); source=''generated'' builds one from a protocols recipe (set protocol_slug only). To cancel: UPDATE ... SET skip = true (never DELETE a row that is already scheduled). Editing a row after approval voids the approval. Leave status, schedule_id, resolved_workout_id and enacted_date alone — the enactor owns them. Done or not: join activities on (raw->>''workoutId'')::bigint = resolved_workout_id and (raw->>''startTimeLocal'')::date = enacted_date.';

comment on table protocols is
'Workout recipes the coach may author for source=''generated'' plan rows. Editing a protocol voids approvals of plan rows that use it (use a new slug when the session changes). Two kinds:
(1) kind=''strength'' — guided Garmin Strength workout, one exercise at a time. params: {"warmup": "lap" (default) or null, "exercises": [{"category": "PULL_UP", "exercise": "WEIGHTED_PULL_UP", "sets": 4, "reps": 3, "weight_kg": 10, "rest_s": 180, "note": "full lockout"}, {"category": "PLANK", "exercise": "PLANK", "sets": 3, "time_s": 45}]}. Each exercise: category + exercise from exercise_catalog (required), sets >= 1, exactly one of reps / time_s, optional weight_kg (> 0, added load), rest_s in seconds (omit = rest until lap button), note <= 50 chars shown on the watch (use "L"/"R" with two consecutive entries for per-side work). No supersets/pyramids. Unknown keys or exercises are refused at upload.
HANGBOARD SESSIONS USE THIS KIND so the hung load is recorded per set: one entry per grip/edge with {"category": "CARRY", "exercise": "BAR_HOLDS", "sets": 3, "time_s": 10, "rest_s": 60, "weight_kg": 6, "note": "half crimp 4F · 20mm"} — time_s = hang length, sets = number of hangs, rest_s = rest between hangs, weight_kg = added load, note = the real grip and edge. Name the protocol so it is obviously hangboarding (e.g. "Max hangs 10s — half crimp"). For %-of-max prescriptions: load = % × (bodyweight + max added load) − bodyweight, bodyweight from the latest daily_metrics.weigh_in; if that is negative (assisted), omit weight_kg and write the assistance in the note (e.g. "half crimp 4F · −6 kg pulley"). Afterwards activity_exercise_set_rows shows each hang as exercise BAR_HOLDS with its actual weight_kg — in this project BAR_HOLDS means a hangboard hang.
(2) kind=''other'' — plain interval timer on Garmin''s ''Other'' sport, for UNWEIGHTED intervals only (records no per-set load): warm-up (ends on lap button), reps × (work_s on / rest_s off), cool-down (lap button). params (seconds): {"work_s": 7, "rest_s": 3, "reps": 6}, optional "warmup_s"/"cooldown_s" (default 300); keep "sets" at 1 (multi-set not verified yet).
name and description are what the athlete sees on the watch. For runs, rides etc. there is no generator: schedule an existing library workout (training_plan.source=''library'') instead.';
